{
  "id": "Lyo.Algorithms.Sqlite",
  "name": "Lyo.Algorithms.Sqlite",
  "area": "Data",
  "tagline": "SQLite catalog for Lyo.Algorithms. Same store contract as Postgres, for a single writer.",
  "description": "IAlgorithmDefinitionStore on a SQLite file. Table names match the Postgres catalog without a schema, including the optional payload column on revisions. A unique revision conflict is retried once. Migrations go through Lyo.Sqlite. The store implements IHealth with SELECT 1. Multi-instance hosts should use Lyo.Algorithms.Postgres instead.",
  "features": [
    "**Options.** SqliteAlgorithmOptions (section SqliteAlgorithms) implements ISqliteMigrationConfig. ConnectionString is required.",
    "**DI.** AddSqliteAlgorithmStore, the Action overload, and AddSqliteAlgorithmStoreFromConfiguration register the store and IHealth."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register a file database",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddAlgorithms();\nservices.AddSqliteAlgorithmStore(new SqliteAlgorithmOptions { ConnectionString = \"Data Source=./algorithms.db\" });"
    }
  ],
